  exp: "The slide demonstrates transitional epithelium (urothelium), which exclusively lines the urinary tract from the minor calyces of the kidney, renal pelvis, ureters, urinary bladder, and the proximal prostatic urethra. Its superficial dome-shaped 'umbrella' (facet) cells contain rigid asymmetric unit membrane plaques composed of uroplakin proteins connected by flexible hinge regions. When the urinary bladder distends with urine, these apical plaques unfold and the epithelium flattens from 5–6 layers to 2–3 apparent layers without rupturing its tight junctions, maintaining an osmotic barrier against hypertonic urine.",
