  q: "A medical student is asked to identify four unlabeled H&E histology slides taken from different regions of the human gastrointestinal tract. On Slide 2, he observes leaf-shaped intestinal villi lined by simple columnar epithelium with goblet cells, crypts of Lieberkühn in the lamina propria, and prominent branched tubuloacinar mucous glands completely filling the SUBMUCOSA beneath the muscularis mucosae. Which segment of the gastrointestinal tract is shown on Slide 2?",
